## PROMPT 2 — Module 2 · Living Plan

```
Build the /plan page. Its job is to prove the plan is maintained state that
re-decides on incoming signals, not a monthly artefact.

LAYOUT: two columns, 60/40.

LEFT — "Current plan" (the artefact)
A card titled with the hero account name and cycle. Inside, a table with columns:
  SEQ · WHO ENGAGES · OBJECTIVE · WINDOW · STATUS
Rows are claims joined from data.claims + live status. Row treatment:
  - scheduled  → white row, teal left bar, sequence number shown in serif
  - routed     → pale violet row, violet left bar, sequence shows "—",
                 status text "ROUTED · FIREWALL TRACK"
  - suppressed → pale warm row, red left bar, sequence "—", text at 85% opacity
Beneath the table, a panel "Every line carries its reason" listing the reason
for each non-scheduled line, referencing the rule id and its plain-English text
from policy.tieBreakRules / hardConstraints.

Above the table: a capacity meter — N of M touches used, as a segmented bar
(one segment per available touch), plus a separate small marker for the
firewalled track that is explicitly NOT counted against the commercial ceiling.

RIGHT — "Signal feed" and controls
A "Run month" button. On click, replay data.signals in tOffsetSec order,
compressed into roughly 40 seconds. Each signal animates into the feed as a
compact card: day label, type chip, headline, detail.
Then, based on signal.effect:
  - "replan"        → the left table reorders with a 250ms transition, the plan
                      version counter increments, and a toast reads
                      "Plan re-decided · v{n}" with signal.narrative beneath
  - "no-change"     → the signal card gets a muted "Below re-decision threshold
                      — plan holds" tag and NOTHING on the left moves.
                      THIS IS IMPORTANT. It proves there is a decision threshold
                      rather than reflexive churn. Do not skip it.
  - "capacity-debit"→ the capacity meter debits one segment with a brief pulse
  - "firewall-track"→ the routed row updates; commercial rows are untouched,
                      with a small note "no effect on commercial sequence by design"

VERSION HISTORY
A horizontal version strip above the plan: v1 · v2 · v3, from data.planVersions.
Clicking a version renders the plan AS AT that version, read-only, with a
banner "Viewing v{n} — {trigger}" and a "Return to current" action. Scrubbing
backwards must work. This is what separates a plan from a feed.

ESCALATION
When a re-decision would displace an already-scheduled claim, do not apply it
silently. Show an inline amber bar: "Re-decision crosses a threshold — requires
enterprise owner confirmation" with Confirm / Defer buttons. Confirm applies the
change and writes a decision record. This keeps the autonomy story consistent.

Speed control: 1x / 2x / instant. Provide a Reset that restores v1 cleanly.
```

